{
  "title": "Web: extract a shared recipe-form state hook (form state \
hand-wired 3x, ~30-prop RecipeForm)",
  "description": "ramekin-ui/src/components/RecipeForm.tsx:34-89 declares a \
~30-member props interface (16 field accessor/setter pairs). \
pages/CreateRecipePage.tsx:31-49 and pages/EditRecipePage.tsx:20-38 each \
independently declare the same ~18 form signals, and both duplicate the \
photo-upload/remove/paste handlers (CreateRecipePage.tsx:138-166, \
EditRecipePage.tsx:88-132) and the request-serialization block \
(CreateRecipePage.tsx:182-194, EditRecipePage.tsx:140-161).\n\
\n\
Fix: introduce a createRecipeFormState() hook returning a single store + \
serializer + photo handlers; collapse RecipeForm to 1-2 props and delete ~150 \
duplicated lines across the two pages.\n\
\n\
Web-only by design: iOS has its own analogous form-view-model issue \
(p4-ios-list-and-form-view-models); no shared deterministic logic is \
introduced, so no vector/parity work is needed here.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
